Z||000000||camon||12-04-2001||01:07 PM||||I'm gonna look into getting my car painted in the next few weeks (either yellow or a dark gray) and was wondering how much you guys (that had your cars painted) spent to get your paint jobs done!<P>I was thinking about trying maaco but have heard some horor stories about there paint jobs (in regards to quality) are they as bad as some say? <BR>Is it possible to get a descent looking paint job for around 500.00 (give or take a 100.00 or so)? <BR>How much did you spend on your paint job and were you satisfied with the end result!<P>------------------<BR>   Keith<BR>1987 Fiero GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||12-04-2001||01:50 PM||||check out the Maaco around you and look at their paint finish, not the prep. If their painter is good, he can do a great job. The low price paint shops really fall down on prep, sanding and taping. If you prep it yourself, you can get a nice job. I own a body shop and I send my dealers cars to them to spray. tape everything but the windows yourself. On the windows, just run a strip of 3/4 tape all around the edges so all they have to do is stick paper on windows. A decent paint job will cost upwards of $1,000. A great, wet sanded and rubbed job around $2000 and up.||||reg||1
